BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU Asian Culture Center
DTSTART:20260929T160000Z
DTEND:20260929T170000Z
LOCATION:Asian Culture Center (807 E 10th street\, Bloomington\, IN)
SUMMARY:Student Development Series/Workshop "Budgeting 101" by IU MoneySm
 arts
DESCRIPTION:This&#160\;interactive presentation is designed to help under
 graduate students build a strong foundation in money management while nav
 igating college life. Students will learn the basics of creating a budget
 \, understanding income and expenses\, and developing practical strategie
 s to manage money throughout the semester. The session explores topics su
 ch as financial aid refunds\, saving habits\, budgeting with changing inc
 ome\, and common financial challenges students experience in college. Par
 ticipants will leave with simple tools\, resources\, and actionable tips 
 to help them make informed financial decisions and build healthy financia
 l habits that support both their academic and personal success.  &#160\; 
  All Indiana University events\, groups\, activities\, and&#160\;educatio
 nal\, cultural\, and historical observances welcome all IU students and o
 ther members of the Indiana University community.For more information\, v
 iew this event in BeInvolved (https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/124766
 32).
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  This<strong>&#160\;</strong>interactive
  presentation is designed to help undergraduate students build a strong f
 oundation in money management while navigating college life. Students wil
 l learn the basics of creating a budget\, understanding income and expens
 es\, and developing practical strategies to manage money throughout the s
 emester. The session explores topics such as financial aid refunds\, savi
 ng habits\, budgeting with changing income\, and common financial challen
 ges students experience in college. Participants will leave with simple t
 ools\, resources\, and actionable tips to help them make informed financi
 al decisions and build healthy financial habits that support both their a
 cademic and personal success.</p><br /><p>  &#160\;</p><br /><p>  All Ind
 iana University events\, groups\, activities\, and&#160\;educational\, cu
 ltural\, and historical observances welcome all IU students and other mem
 bers of the Indiana University community.</p><br /><strong>For more infor
