BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU Asian Culture Center
DTSTART:20261105T220000Z
DTEND:20261105T230000Z
LOCATION:Asian Culture Center (807 E 10th street\, Bloomington\, IN)
SUMMARY:ACC's Over A Cup of Tea presents Aesthetics of the Cute: Globaliz
 ation of East Asian Kawaii Culture by Haoxuan Gao
DESCRIPTION:From Hello Kitty's global empire to Labubu and K-pop idols\, 
 "cute" has become one of East Asia's most powerful and contested cultural
  exports. This session frames "cuteness" as an aesthetic category\, traci
 ng kawaii culture's root in postwar Japan\, and its journey into global p
 op culture. A harder question follows: What gets flattened or fetishized 
 when cuteness travels across cultures? This event will be facilitated by 
 Haoxuan Gao\, a Sociology PhD student at IU Bloomington who studies cultu
 re\, modernity\, and social psychology.&#160\;  &#160\;  All Indiana Univ
 ersity events\, groups\, activities\, and&#160\;educational\, cultural\, 
 and historical observances welcome all IU students and other members of t
 he Indiana University community.For more information\, view this event in
  BeInvolved (https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12476676).
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><span data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">
 From Hello Kitty's global empire to Labubu and K-pop idols\, "cute" has b
 ecome one of East Asia's most powerful and contested cultural exports. Th
 is session frames "cuteness" as an aesthetic category\, tracing kawaii cu
 lture's root in postwar Japan\, and its journey into global pop culture. 
 A harder question follows: What gets flattened or fetishized when cutenes
 s travels across cultures? This event will be facilitated by Haoxuan Gao\
 , a Sociology PhD student at IU Bloomington who studies culture\, moderni
 ty\, and social psychology.&#160\;</span></p><br /><p>  &#160\;</p><br />
 <p>  All Indiana University events\, groups\, activities\, and&#160\;educ
 ational\, cultural\, and historical observances welcome all IU students a
 nd other members of the Indiana University community.</p><br /><strong>Fo
 r more information\, <a href="https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/124766
 76">view this event in BeInvolved</a>.</strong>
